   127	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   128	    """
   129	    Count the complete green 2x2 diagnosis blocks and use that count as the zoom factor for the upper pattern.
   130	
   131	    Input structure:
   132	    - The background is black.
   133	    - One full grey row separates the grid into an upper pattern region and a lower diagnosis region.
   134	    - The upper region contains one small multicolor pattern in blue, red, green, and yellow on black.
   135	    - The lower region contains scattered red and green objects, including some complete green 2x2 squares and distractors.
   136	
   137	    Rule:
   138	    - Find the unique full grey separator row and split the grid above and below it.
   139	    - Crop the upper region to the bounding box of its non-black pattern pixels.
   140	    - In the lower region, inspect only green 4-connected components and keep only those whose bounding box is exactly 2x2 and whose area is exactly 4.
   141	    - Let N be the number of such complete green squares, then replace each cropped pattern pixel with an N x N solid block of the same color.
   142	    - Output only the enlarged cropped pattern.
   143	
